    {
      "id": "AUDIT-008-001",
      "path": "src/client/java/dev/hylfrd/farmhelper/client/platform/ClientTickAdapter.java",
      "severity": "HIGH",
      "summary": "The client adapter did not normalize trusted vanilla system messages to the parser's system channel.",
      "upstream_behavior": "The fixed Minecraft 26.1.2 client packet boundary routes ClientboundSystemChatPacket through ClientPacketListener.handleSystemChat; Fabric API 0.153.0+26.1.2 exposes that route through GAME with overlay=false, while CHAT is player-sent and GAME also covers ordinary server game messages.",
      "incompatibility": "ClientTickAdapter mapped every non-overlay GAME callback to 'game' and emitted no 'system' channel, so the client never supplied the parser with the trusted source label for the production Limbo line. Parser-side system-only enforcement is an AUDIT-002 dependency and is not present in this tree.",
      "replacement": "Prepare the parser contract by scoping the fixed system-packet callback in ClientPacketListenerMixin and capturing the trusted channel before ClientTickAdapter dispatch. Normalize only a non-overlay GAME callback inside that scope to 'system'; keep player CHAT as 'chat', ordinary GAME as 'game', and overlay GAME as 'overlay'.",
      "resolution_scope": "ADAPTER_ONLY",
      "cross_item_dependencies": [
        "AUDIT-002: the current tree's GameStateParser does not enforce the system-only channel contract; AUDIT-002 PR #6 must add and verify that parser-side fail-closed enforcement."
      ],
      "closure_note": "AUDIT-008-001 is resolved for the client adapter boundary in this PR. This report does not claim whole-product system-message enforcement or close AUDIT-002.",
      "automated_evidence": [
        "ClientTickAdapterTest.normalizesOnlyTheFixedSystemPacketScopeAsTrusted proves chat, generic game, overlay, scoped system, and scope cleanup channels.",
        "ClientTickAdapterTest.systemScopeRestoresOnThrownHandlerAndNestedReentry proves original-handler and callback exception cleanup, nested scope isolation, one-shot trusted delivery, outer-scope restoration, and post-scope marker clearance.",
        "WorldTransitionParserSequenceTest.stableReplacementUnloadLoadChatResetAndDisconnectKeepExactLocationPriority exercises the adapter's trusted system channel in the replacement sequence; it does not prove parser-side channel enforcement.",
        "AUDIT-002 parser-side system-only enforcement is an explicit cross-item dependency and is not evidenced by this tree.",
